Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 5 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 7): THE PAPER'S COUNT OF RETRACTIONS IS THE
 INDEX'S AGAIN, AND ITS TEST IS ONE A LANDING RUNS

Sent back with R80a: tests/test_b1425_determinism.py::test_the_papers_retraction_count_matches_the_index
fails at main's head. Main's word: its own fault, and older than that day. The paper gives the length of the
retractions index in words, "seventy-nine"; the index has 97 rows; the test's table of number words stops at
80, so the test stopped there and said to extend the table. Main counted the index at four commits: it passed
80 rows inside Review 79's window, and no landing since ran this test.

The mend, as main states it:
  - the paper's count is brought to the index's, as an erratum of a count, the way it was last done on
    2026-11-04: one word in papers/P3_THE_PAPER/main.tex and the same word in the generator that emits the
    sentence. It reads ninety-seven. Nothing else of the paper is touched;
  - the table of words is extended well past the present length: a number is spelt out, to 999, and the
    spelling is held to every word the table had. The table as it stood is kept;
  - the test joins the tests a landing runs: the selector of those tests names the file, beside the gate
    runner. It was in the selection only because its text happens to hold a word the selector's pattern looks
    for. A test holds that a change to the index selects it, and that a change to the paper or to its
    generator asks for the full suite.

One thing more, found on the way and mended: the test's pattern for the paper's count took one hyphenated
word. From 100 rows the count is several words ("one hundred and four"), and the pattern would have found no
count at all. The index stands three rows from that.

The lock keeps its meaning: the paper's count is the index's, and the generator's sentence is the paper's.

Run: the 17 test files that read the paper, its generator, the index or the selector. On the commit before: 1
failed, 101 passed, 1 skipped. On the patch: 103 passed, 1 skipped. Every gate passes but the count of
landings.

The log's entry for this erratum is main's to write. Main's fault by main's word; the count of 97 is the
test's own count of the index.

BUILT AGAIN ON MAIN'S 663a902ff (2026-11-13): main had mended the same count on its own head since (the paper and its
generator read "one hundred", and the test's table of number words is extended by main). This patch keeps main's paper,
generator and table, and does not touch them. What it still brings: the test's pattern takes a count of several words
("one hundred and four"), held by a sentence of its own; and the selector of the tests a landing runs names this test,
with the test that holds it. The test file passes (16).
